Project NOMAD
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The SIGA AI module (`src/features/siga-ai`, `src/lib/siga-ai`) contains work
derived from Project NOMAD by Crosstalk Solutions, LLC:

    https://github.com/Crosstalk-Solutions/project-nomad
    Commit 54ee30a44902e5c252b477f8685c26ec3064ab72 (v1.35.1)
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

What was derived, and the changes made:

  * Retrieval parameters, chunking strategy, embedding-model choice and task
    prefixes, reranking heuristic, relevance floor and model-size context tiers,
    ported from `admin/constants/ollama.ts` and
    `admin/app/services/rag_service.ts` into
    `src/features/siga-ai/nomad-params.ts`, `chunking.ts`, `rerank.ts` and
    `context-limits.ts`. Provenance is recorded per parameter in those files.
  * The Ollama HTTP contract — endpoint order and the `/api/embed` to
    `/v1/embeddings` fallback — ported from `admin/app/services/ollama_service.ts`
    into `src/lib/siga-ai/ollama-client.server.ts`. Reimplemented over the
    standard `fetch` API; no NOMAD source code is redistributed verbatim.
  * The shape of the RAG system prompt, from `SYSTEM_PROMPTS.rag_context`,
    adapted in `src/features/siga-ai/prompts.ts` to Angolan Portuguese, to
    school profiles, and with an added rule that treats retrieved documents as
    untrusted data rather than instructions.

Changes relative to Project NOMAD: single-tenant and unauthenticated access was
replaced by Supabase authentication, school membership checks, per-school vector
isolation and audit logging; the global `nomad_knowledge_base` collection was
replaced by `siga_ai_kb` with a mandatory `school_id` filter; persistence moved
from SQLite to PostgreSQL with server-only access.

Ollama and Qdrant are consumed as external services and are not redistributed
with this software.
